    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.2207v1</id>
    <title>On Sun's conjecture concerning disjoint cosets</title>
    <updated>2008-07-14T16:58:40Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.2207v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0807.2207v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  In 2004, Zhi-Wei Sun posed the following conjecture: If a_1G_1,...,a_kG_k (k&gt;1) are finitely many pairwise disjoint left cosets in a group G with all the indices [G:G_i] finite, then for some 1\le i&lt;j\le k, the greatest common divisor of [G:G_i] and [G:G_j] is at least k. In this paper, we confirm Sun's conjecture for k=3,4.</summary>
